            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there a change in phosphor-post-codes to support the backend for this?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "`Boot.Raw` will be set by phosphor-host-ipmid.\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-host-ipmid/+/78109"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 30,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Redfish service validator tests?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 30,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes. It pass Redfish-service-validator."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 30,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please put that in your commit message tested statement."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 30,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Overall, seems like a feature we could support, but needs some code cleanup."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 763,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We should not be depending on a specific value on dbus to chain another dbus operation.  Chaining in that way leads to slow APIs.\n\nWhat I suspect its that the second query can be done unconditionally."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 763,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "According to Redfish schema[1], it mentioned that `OemLastState` shall only be present if `LastState` is `OEM`. So I think it depends on OEM state.\n\n[1] https://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/ComputerSystem.v1_23_1.json"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 763,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure, then query the two values together (using getProperties) and you can enforce that constraint without chaining dbus calls."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 763,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "They come from different dbus object and interface. Is it possible to query them together by using getAllProperties?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 792,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please do not invent new hex conversion functions.  Please use the the ones that exist already."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 792,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 794,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Given this is an oem parameter, value needs prefixed with the openbmc OEM namespace, so something like\n\n\"OpenBMC 0X20\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 794,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 795,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "No lambdas over 3 lines please"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 795,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
